course: dictionary
lesson: 5572
title: Lethal and its clues
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words sound scary, and the context tells you how scary. «A lethal snake bite» is a bite that can cause death. You can tell from the words around it: snake and bite are both dangerous things, so lethal must mean deadly.
explain: Look for small word parts too. In «Less-lethal weapon», the word less tells you the weapon is not as deadly as a normal one. The entry says it is meant not to kill, such as a rubber bullet, but it can still kill, so it is not completely safe.
explain: Lethal can also be slang in sport. A «lethal» player is not one who causes death. It means someone who scores a lot and is very dangerous to the other team. Always ask what fits the sentence, then check your meaning by swapping it in.
fact: Lethal is an adjective. It means able to kill; deadly.
fact: «A lethal dose» means an amount of medicine or poison that can cause death.
fact: In informal talk, «a lethal shot» means a very accurate and dangerous shot.
fact: Deadly is a close synonym of lethal, but lethal is more formal and is often used in news and science.
fact: Less-lethal means not meant to kill, but it can still cause death, as with a rubber bullet.
exercise: «The guide warned us that the snake's bite was lethal.» What does lethal mean? | *Able to kill | Very tasty | Slightly warm
exercise: In football, a «lethal» striker scores a lot of goals. What does lethal suggest here? | Very sleepy and slow | Able to kill | *Very effective and dangerous to the other team
exercise: «Less-lethal weapon» means a weapon that is... | Certain to kill | *Not meant to kill, though it can still kill | Harmless and cannot hurt anyone | Made only for play
test: Which word is closest in meaning to lethal? | Gentle | Sleepy | *Deadly
test: Why does the word less in «less-lethal weapon» matter? | It shows the weapon is the most powerful ever made | It means the weapon is made of wood | *It shows the weapon is not as deadly, but it can still kill | It means the weapon can never hurt anyone
exam: In «a lethal dose» of medicine, what does lethal tell you? | *The dose is enough to cause death | The dose is a small amount that is safe | The dose tastes sweet | The dose is given at dinner time
